WHAT THIS COVERS

The curriculum itself, wherever it appears — including inside index.html,
where most of it lives as JavaScript data:

  * lesson structure, objectives and stage sequencing
  * exercises, their answers, and their explanations
  * vocabulary entries and example sentences
  * reading texts and dialogues
  * grammar articles
  * cultural notes
  * the same content, re-extracted as JSON for the free-writing feedback
    agent: agent/grounding/vocab.json, grammar.json, verbs.json, and
    gloss_index.json

The software that renders it, and the software that reads it (including the
agent code under agent/), is separately licensed under MIT. See LICENSE.


