WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER

  * THE AUDIO. audio/ and audio-manifest.js are absent from this repository
    by design. They are generated from Google Translate's text-to-speech
    endpoint, which is undocumented and not licensed for redistribution.
    They are a local build artifact, are not distributed here, and are not
    licensed by this file or any other. Regenerate them yourself with
    tools/fetch_audio.py, and read docs/AUDIO.md first — including the note
    on what a redistributable alternative would cost.

  * QUOTED OFFICIAL TEXTS, which were never mine to license. The
    Constitution of Romania (Article 1, in the citizenship track), the oath
    of allegiance, and the national anthem "Deșteaptă-te, române!" by Andrei
    Mureșanu (1848) are reproduced as public/official texts. Under Romanian
    Law 8/1996 art. 9, official texts fall outside copyright.

  * THE EMBEDDED VIDEOS. Six YouTube videos are embedded by reference. They
    belong to their creators and are subject to YouTube's terms. Nothing is
    copied or redistributed here.


SOURCES AND ATTRIBUTION

The original course content in this repository was independently written.
External sources informed its design and were used for reference and
verification as described below:
  
  * Institutul Limbii Române publishes sample papers for the B1 attestation.
    The ILR track is built around the format, question types and marking
    those papers reveal. The available machine-readable source material is 
    checked for verbatim reuse by tools/check_reuse.py; the current audit 
    reports no unwaived matches at its six-word comparison threshold.

  * "Learn Romanian Manual" (Dr. Mona Moldoveanu Pologea, ROLANG) and
    "Limba Română" (Grigore Brâncuș) were read as background. Their sequencing 
    and choice of contrasts informed the course, but their prose was not 
    intentionally reproduced. Note one honest gap: the Brâncuș volume is 
    a scanned PDF with no text layer, so the automated check could not read it.
  
  * Wiktionary was used only as a verification reference by
    tools/verify_verbs.py. No Wiktionary text is intentionally reproduced in
    the course content. Wiktionary's own content remains subject to its
    applicable licenses.
